File: lib/OCP/Drift.pm:244

```perl
my $list = eval { $self->api->list('Node') } or return;
```

When the Kubernetes API call throws (auth revoked, 5xx, TLS, RBAC denied), the whole distribution_drift pass silently returns undef. `ocp status` then prints a green drift summary saying every component matches, while the actual reason nothing was compared was a transient API failure. No warn, no log, no status row that says "could not query kubelet versions".

Replace the bare `eval` with explicit error reporting — log the failure and surface it in the drift table, same as karr #106 demands for any eval-guarded k8s call.

Repro:
1. Point OCP_DRIFT_API at a kubeconfig with a revoked token
2. ocp status
Observed: prints a green drift summary with no warning.
